{
  "note": "HAND-AUTHORED, NOT RECORDED. No archive node produced these bytes. Every result word was packed by hand from the integers the phase-4 golden fixtures already pin, by a throwaway script that imports nothing from auradefi, and the ten selectors were derived from an independent keccak256 and cross-checked against the literals the abi and reader orders pin. The file therefore proves the selector derivation, the word packing, the tuple decode, the block pin and the JSON-RPC wire path. It does NOT prove agreement with Ethereum mainnet at block 20,450,000: two of the preimages cannot come from a node at all (a fabricated Aave user, and a protocol-global rETH exchange rate no choice of holder can make a node return). Obtaining a genuine archive-node recording at that block and re-pinning every existing golden to whatever it returns needs network and an archive node, and it is a separate human task. The per-interaction 'note' and 'request.body' keys are ignored by auradefi.testing.cassettes.load, so this stays one cassette format while carrying what the JSON-RPC matcher in tests/golden/test_phase11_reader.py keys on.",
